<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battus I of Cyrene</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Battus I was the founder and first king of Cyrene in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, who, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, led settlers from the island of Thera there around 631 BCE on the advice of the Delphic oracle. He ruled for about 40 years and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battiad-dynasty">Battiad dynasty</a>, whose kings were alternately named Battus and Arcesilaus until the monarchy ended around 440 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battus-i-of-cyrene.jpg" alt="Battus I of Cyrene" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillaume de L'Isle · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royaume_de_Tripoli_1707.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
